dist/*
defaultTheme/*

# Two files are tracked explicitly rather than by pattern, and both had to be, because
# `defaultTheme/*` ignored everything and the effect was invisible:
#
#   - `dist.tar.zst` is the theme's build output. It comes from a **separate repository** (the
#     LuminaPlus theme) whose sources this one does not contain, so CI cannot produce it. Before these
#     exceptions the archive was ignored and therefore never committed, and CI and the release workflow
#     each rebuilt it inline from `frontend/dist` plus `frontend/komari-theme.json` -- the panel's own
#     UI, described by komari-web's manifest. The embedded default theme was quietly the panel's
#     built-in interface, and a change to it was discarded on the next build.
#   - `komari-theme.json` was ignored too, so **CI did not have it either**, and the same workflows
#     created it on the spot by copying `frontend/komari-theme.json`. That is why the identity test
#     reported the previous theme even after the file in the working tree had been replaced: what CI
#     embedded was never what the repository held.
#
# Everything else under defaultTheme/ stays ignored, because everything else is generated.
#
# `script/embed-theme.mjs` checks both during CI and regenerates the archive with `--write`;
# docs/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md records the theme version and the licence obligation.
!defaultTheme/dist.tar.zst
!defaultTheme/komari-theme.json
